 "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by about two points. She holds a clear cash advantage over Republican Carrie Buck, a state senator who has raised a competitive sum but trails in money on hand. No independent or third-party candidate appears to be a factor.\n\nPublic polling of the race is absent, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert assessments. Most forecasters rate the race Likely Democratic, with several calling it Safe or Solid, and prediction markets put Titus's chances in the low-to-mid nineties. Republicans hope the 'no tax on tips' issue and Buck's profile can keep this competitive, but the evidence so far favors the incumbent by a comfortable, if not overwhelming, margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}]}